P = dict(
 title="Snowboarding: Privacy Policy", desc="Snowboarding privacy policy: no data collection, no account, no ads, no tracking.",
 h1="Snowboarding: Privacy Policy", sub="Effective November 3, 2026",
 short_label="In short",
 short="The app does not collect personal data. Everything you mark and write stays on your iPhone. No account, no ads, no analytics, no tracking. The app works offline.",
 sections=[
  ("What the app stores on your device","Your chosen language, stance and experience, your haptics, sound and control settings, lessons completed in the app, your observations, saved cues, personal notes and best game scores. The app never sends this data anywhere. It may be included in your iPhone backup if you have backups turned on."),
  ("Motion sensors and camera","In the lessons, if you turn on tilt control, and during rides in the game, the app reads the phone’s tilt and movement to steer the board on screen. These values are not stored or sent anywhere. The camera and microphone are not used: the game’s sounds are generated inside the app. Location and Health data are not used."),
  ("Purchase","The one-time purchase is handled by Apple. We never receive your payment details, and the app only learns whether the full version has been bought."),
  ("What we do not do","We do not collect, sell or share personal data. The app has no third-party SDKs, ads or analytics. It makes no network requests of its own."),
  ("Deleting your data","Settings → Reset practice history removes your progress or all practice data. Deleting the app removes all of its data from the device."),
  ("Children","The app is made for adult beginners and does not collect data about anyone."),
  ("Changes","If this policy changes, the new version will be published at this address with a new date.")],
 contact_h="Contact",
)
S = dict(
 title="Snowboarding: Support", desc="Snowboarding support and frequently asked questions.",
 h1="Snowboarding: Support", sub="We reply within 48 hours",
 cards=[("Contact us","Questions, bugs, feedback","Send email","Snowboarding"),("Report a bug","Include your iPhone model and iOS version","Report","Snowboarding bug report")],
 faq_h="Frequently asked questions",
 faq=[("Where do I start?","Open the Lessons tab and start with level one: the rules on the slope and how to fall and get up. The levels suggest an order."),
  ("How do I steer the ball by tilting the phone?","In the turn lessons choose “Ride it yourself”, turn on “Control with phone tilt” and press Start. Hold the phone flat like a small board: tip the top away from you for toes, toward you for heels. You can also steer with a finger."),
  ("How does the purchase work?","The app is a one-time purchase with no subscription. Details are on its App Store page."),
  ("How do I restore my purchase?","On a new iPhone with the same Apple Account, open Settings → Restore purchase."),
  ("How do I control the game?","Tilt left or right to put the board on its edge. Tip the top away for more speed. A finger on the screen squats, and letting go jumps. In the air, tilt spins and flips, and a finger grabs. In detail: Game tab → How to control."),
  ("The board drifts to one side. What can I do?","The phone’s position during the countdown becomes neutral. Pause, hold the phone comfortably and tap Continue: the countdown sets it again. If tilt doesn’t suit you, turn it off in the Game tab’s settings and steer with a finger."),
  ("How do I turn off the sound?","The iPhone’s silent mode mutes the game’s sounds, and Game tab → Wind and edge sounds turns them off. Your music keeps playing."),
  ("How do I find my stance?","The app asks which foot leads. If you’re not sure, choose “I don’t know yet” and it shows an example stance, clearly labeled. You can change it in Settings. Your writing hand doesn’t decide your stance."),
  ("Does the app rate my riding?","No. The scenes are simplified teaching models. The app doesn’t use the camera and can’t see how you ride. Finishing a lesson in the app doesn’t mean you can do the move safely on snow."),
  ("Do I need the internet?","No. All content is built into the app, and no account is needed."),
  ("How do I change the language?","Settings → Language: system default or one of nine languages. It applies immediately."),
  ("How do I reset my progress?","Settings → Reset practice history. You can reset progress only, or everything."),
  ("Which devices are supported?","iPhone with iOS 18 or later.")],
)
